I"<p>With a team of 3 others I had never met before, we built a full-stack application that helps users model the damage a potential hurricane could cause. We wanted to make hurricane risk easier to understand, so the app lets users draw a storm path, select their location, and compare likely outcomes through maps and generated statistics.</p>

<p>This project won the Knight Hacks 2023 Best Use of Google Cloud category.</p>

<p>The following technologies were used in the making of this project:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Google Maps API</li>
  <li>JavaScript/HTML/CSS</li>
  <li>Google Maps Visualization, Places, and Drawing Libraries</li>
  <li>Node.js</li>
  <li>Google Maps Heatmap</li>
  <li>ChatGPT integration to query hurricane statistics</li>
</ul>

